// ============================================================================
//  mod_tac45.zone  -  the Tac-45, weapon 12 and the last multiplayer pistol.
//
//  User request, 2026-08-16: "The Tac-45 pistol needs to be added to the mystery
//  box weapon addition like all the other weapons ported from the multiplayer,
//  i just realised that's the only weapon missing. Make sure all the required fx
//  both visual and audio wise are working for it, no exceptions."
//
//  🌟 THE DEF IS `fnp45`, NOT `tac45`. Black Ops II ships this gun under its
//  development name - the real-world FNP-45 Tactical it is modelled on - in the
//  weapon def, the art, the camo, the HUD material and every sound alias. The
//  release name "Tac-45" appears only in the localized string. Same trap the
//  XPR-50 sprang (def `as50`, art `xpr50`), and it was settled the same way:
//  BO2-Reimagined ships weapons\zm\fnp45_zm, and grepping the fastfile index for
//  "tac45" finds only two loose MP menu .dds in the IPAK dump. [[t6-asset-vs-def-name-mismatch]]
//
//  🛑 IT IS DUAL-WIELD WHEN PACK-A-PUNCHED, so THREE defs ship, not two:
//        fnp45_zm              dualWield 0, playerAnimType default
//        fnp45_upgraded_zm     dualWield 1, playerAnimType dualwield,
//                              DualWieldWeapon = fnp45lh_upgraded_zm
//        fnp45lh_upgraded_zm   dualWield 1, inventoryType dwlefthand,
//                              DualWieldWeapon = fnp45_upgraded_zm
//  The two upgraded defs point at each other, so both must ship or neither
//  resolves. This is the same shape as stock's Mustang & Sally
//  (m1911_upgraded_zm / m1911lh_upgraded_zm), which this project already ships -
//  checked rather than assumed, and that pair needs no attachmentunique either.
//  Only fnp45_zm may be a box result; the left-hand half is included as a
//  variant, exactly like the Titus-6's alt-fire half.
//
//  📝 NO PACK-A-PUNCH ATTACHMENT ROW NEEDED. All three defs have an EMPTY
//  `attachments` field - the same shape as mk48 / insas / crossbow / titus6 - so
//  add_attachments() has nothing to look up and the v1.89.3 freeze cannot apply.
//  For the same reason no attachmentunique is required, unlike the XPR-50.
//
//  📝 THE PACK-A-PUNCH CAMO IS ALREADY CORRECT, unlike the Titus-6's. Measured:
//  camo_fnp45's camoMaterials[3] - the slot zombies uses - already maps
//  mc/mtl_t6_wpn_pistol_fnp45 -> mc/mtl_weapon_camo_zombies. One override, which
//  is Treyarch's own authoring for this gun (camo_sig556 has one too). Nothing to
//  repair.
//
//  WHERE EVERY ASSET COMES FROM
//    all four xmodels, all 71 xanims, camo_fnp45, menu_mp_weapons_fnp45
//        ->  common_mp.ff, which build_ff.bat already --loads (line 339).
//            NO new --load, so the load order and every shared-asset decision
//            it encodes are untouched.
//
//  📝 NOT DECLARED, BECAUSE THEY ALREADY RESOLVE ON EVERY ZOMBIES MAP. Checked
//  one by one against an index of all 191 fastfiles in zone\all - each of these
//  is present in zm_transit, zm_buried, zm_tomb, zm_prison, zm_highrise AND
//  zm_nuked:
//        fx,weapon/muzzleflashes/fx_muz_smg_flash_1p / _3p
//        fx,weapon/muzzleflashes_zmb_ug/fx_zmb_muz_sm_gas_flash_1p
//        fx,weapon/muzzleflashes_zmb_ug/fx_zmb_muz_smg_flash_3p
//        fx,weapon/shellejects/fx_pistol
//        fx,temp_effects/fx_tmp_m203_flash
//  and fx,weapon/grenade/fx_trail_grenade is in common_zm. material
//  hud_mp_firerate_single, material reticle_side_small and xmodel
//  projectile_m203grenade are already inside mod.ff.
//
//  📝 NO .iwi ARE STAGED FOR THE GUN. A fastfile carries only image headers, but
//  the XPR-50 and the Titus-6 both ship as bare xmodel declarations out of
//  common_mp / monsoon with no loose .iwi and both render correctly in game, so
//  the pixels reach the renderer from the IPAKs. Precedent, not assumption.
//
//  🔊 THE SOUND HALF IS NOT HERE - it is 54 alias rows in
//  soundbank\mod.all.aliases.additions.csv plus 15 payloads under sound\.
//  See the block above those rows.
// ============================================================================

xmodel,t6_wpn_pistol_fnp45_view
xmodel,t6_wpn_pistol_fnp45_world
xmodel,t6_wpn_pistol_fnp45_view_lh
xmodel,t6_wpn_pistol_fnp45_world_lh

